+<a id="retry-output"></a>
+## Reporting retried test cases
+
+> Introduced in Catch2 X.Y.Z
+
+When [`--retry-failed N`](command-line.md#retrying-failed-test-cases) is
+enabled and a test case is retried, built-in reporters keep diagnostics from
+superseded attempts without letting them change the final result. Their exact
+representations are:
+
+| Reporter | Retry output |
+| --- | --- |
+| console | Marks superseded attempts as `Attempt k of M failed`, identifies the following retry, and reports a flaky pass or exhausted failure explicitly. |
+| compact | Uses the same attempt, retry, flaky-pass, and exhausted-failure messages in compact form. |
+| XML | Wraps every attempt in an `Attempt` element with its number and maximum, followed by an `AttemptResult`; `OverallResult` records attempts used, maximum attempts, and flakiness. |
+| JSON | Adds the attempt number to partial runs and an `attempts` object containing the number used, maximum, flakiness, and per-attempt results. |
+| JUnit | Writes failures from superseded attempts at the start of `system-out`. Only the final attempt can create `failure` or `error` elements and affect suite failure/error counters. |
+| SonarQube | Writes superseded failures as sanitized XML comments. Only the final attempt creates failing elements. |
+| TeamCity | Writes superseded failures as non-failing `testStdErr` messages. Only the final attempt can emit `testFailed`. |
+| TAP | Writes superseded assertions as `#` diagnostic lines that do not consume test-point numbers. Assertions from the final attempt are the numbered test points and determine the plan. |
+| Automake | Writes one result line for the logical test case, based on its final outcome. |
+
+With retries disabled, reporter output is unchanged. With retries enabled but
+unused, only XML and JSON add structural attempt information. TAP buffers its
+own lines until an attempt ends, so those lines can interleave differently
+with output written directly by the test; the TAP text itself is unchanged.
+
+Custom reporters can observe attempts through the
+[`testCaseAttempt` events](reporter-events.md#testcaseattempt-events).
+
+
